{"chunk_id": "dd4455474e0d", "text": "Sugriva sends his minister Hanuman to investigate two mysterious warriors approaching the region of Pampa near Mount Rishyamuka. Leaping down from the mountain, Hanuman disguises himself as a wandering ascetic and respectfully approaches the strangers\u2014Rama and Lakshmana. Speaking with remarkable eloquence, he questions who they are, marveling at their divine appearance, their golden complexions, mighty arms, and formidable weapons. He suggests they seem almost celestial, like the sun and moon descended to earth. Hanuman then reveals his mission: he serves Sugriva, the exiled monkey king who seeks friendship with them. After hearing the speech, Rama is deeply impressed, telling Lakshmana that only someone thoroughly learned in the Vedas and grammar could speak so flawlessly. This moment marks the first meeting between Rama and Hanuman, initiating one of the epic\u2019s most important alliances.\nHanuman, disguised as a monk, approaches Rama and Lakshmana, praises them, and introduces himself as Sugriva\u2019s minister seeking their friendship.\nThemes: first meeting, diplomacy, disguise, alliance formation, eloquence", "vector": [0.014896840788424015, -0.030701374635100365, -0.00124974618665874, -0.00046385772293433547, 0.010465164668858051, 0.030461102724075317, -0.009751023724675179, -0.009690956212580204, -0.019488699734210968, -0.026429880410432816, 0.0027264156378805637, 0.008102493360638618, -0.00505237840116024, 0.0011921811383217573, 0.0021057138219475746, -0.007762108463793993, 0.05077740550041199, -0.02214503474533558, 0.012480776757001877, -0.01585792750120163, 0.003148559480905533, -0.014603176154196262, -0.013975800015032291, -0.0005543767474591732, -0.015831230208277702, 0.009971273131668568, 0.034198664128780365, -0.028885990381240845, 0.0038743801414966583, -0.018861323595046997, -0.005419460125267506, -0.030781466513872147, -0.004324889276176691, 0.001273105968721211, -0.01776675321161747, -0.008843330666422